    <h3>Key Functionalities:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Operational dashboard with monthly hours, billable time, revenue status, alerts, and contract-capacity indicators</li>
        <li>Client directory with contact and business details, active/archived status, and contract history</li>
        <li>Hourly and daily contracts with rates, currencies, validity periods, commitment modes, and allocated budgets</li>
        <li>Daily and weekly time tracking linked to clients and contracts, including billable status and billing snapshots</li>
        <li>Invoice lifecycle tracking with references, issue dates, due dates, payment terms, and voiding support</li>
        <li>Payment recording and visibility into paid, outstanding, and partially settled invoices</li>
        <li>Revenue overview for accrued, expected, forecast, invoiced, paid, and outstanding amounts</li>
        <li>Reports for hours by client, monthly timesheets, contract allocation, and utilization</li>
        <li>Annual invoice and cash reporting with CSV and XLSX exports</li>
        <li>Invoice report exports in CSV, Excel (XLSX), and PDF formats</li>
        <li>Workspace-scoped data access and membership roles</li>
        <li>Email/password authentication, Google OAuth integration, and password recovery workflow</li>
        <li>Workspace settings for timezone, currency, and operational warning thresholds</li>
        <li>System alerts and user notifications for contract, capacity, billing, and payment events</li>
        <li>AI Assistant interface for natural-language questions about workspace analytics</li>
        <li>Layered application architecture with Prisma migrations and automated quality checks</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Operational Dashboard</h3>
    <p>
        The dashboard brings key operational and financial indicators into a single monthly overview. It combines
        worked and billable hours with accrued, invoiced, paid, and outstanding revenue, while highlighting active
        alerts and contract-capacity utilization. This gives freelancers a quick view of delivery activity and cash-flow
        status without switching between separate tools.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e41a147-e8a9-44ef-81db-69223b53548d"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS monthly dashboard" />

    <h3>Weekly Time Tracking</h3>
    <p>
        Time entries can be reviewed in a weekly view and associated with the relevant client and contract. Each entry
        records its date, duration, description, and billable status, supporting a consistent link between work performed
        and the commercial agreement under which it was delivered.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30aa7641-df6a-4888-b9bf-0d3e09091f21"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS weekly time tracking" />

    <h3>Daily Time Tracking</h3>
    <p>
        The daily view provides a more granular way to review and manage individual work entries. It supports day-level
        inspection and entry management while complementing the weekly overview for planning and timesheet review.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/db3505e7-e473-4f2d-8e72-72a320d09b5c"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS daily time tracking" />

    <h3>Client Management</h3>
    <p>
        The client directory centralizes business identity and contact information, including company details and notes.
        Clients can be marked active or archived, and their associated contract history remains available to support
        continuity across engagements.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcfe7163-2d07-42c5-bbe2-bc85a24fa097"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS client directory" />

    <h3>Contract and Commitment Management</h3>
    <p>
        Contracts define the commercial terms of an engagement: hourly or daily billing model, rate, currency, validity
        period, and commitment configuration. Allocation and utilization indicators help make progress against agreed
        capacity visible and connect recorded work to the relevant billing rules.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13fba588-e7a3-41f8-9d02-ad8209ef5b4f"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS contracts overview" />

    <h3>Invoices and Payments</h3>
    <p>
        Invoice tracking provides a consolidated view of billing activity, including invoice references, issue dates,
        amounts, payment terms, and due dates. Payment records allow the application to represent settlement progress
        and distinguish paid, partially paid, overdue, and outstanding amounts where applicable.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2508b9b2-dacf-490c-9123-cd0b28e35942"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS invoices and payment status" />

    <h3>Revenue Analytics and Reports</h3>
    <p>
        Reporting views summarize financial performance across a selected period and break down work by client. Revenue
        indicators distinguish accrued, expected, forecast, invoiced, paid, and outstanding values. Monthly timesheet
        reports and contract utilization tables help connect operational activity to financial outcomes.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93df763f-157f-4d91-84e8-1e8e5ae2aab1"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS reports and analytics" />

    <h3>Notifications and Operational Alerts</h3>
    <p>
        The notification and alert system surfaces operational warnings related to contracts, monthly capacity,
        allocations, invoicing, and payments. These signals help users identify items that may need attention as part
        of their regular workflow.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4ded0c7-cb82-422e-b316-d0ef6bd401be"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="FreelanceOS notifications and alerts" />

    <h3>AI Assistant</h3>
    <p>
        The application includes a conversational interface intended to answer natural-language questions about
        workspace analytics, including revenue, recorded hours, and contracts. AI provider integration is configurable;
        the production provider is not enabled by default, so the interface should not be presented as making live AI
        requests unless the deployment has been explicitly configured to do so.
    </p>

    <h3>Authentication and Workspace Isolation</h3>
    <p>
        Better Auth supports email/password authentication and Google OAuth, alongside the password-recovery workflow.
        Workspace membership and roles provide the application context for operational data, with records scoped to the
        relevant workspace. Initial onboarding guides a new user through workspace creation.
    </p>

    <h3>Workspace Settings</h3>
    <p>
        Workspace settings provide controls for timezone, currency, and warning thresholds used by operational views.
        These settings allow the application to reflect the user's working context and make capacity-related warnings
        more relevant to the workspace.
    </p>

    <h3>Exportable Financial Reports</h3>
    <p>
        Invoice and cash reporting supports exporting data for further analysis and record keeping. Invoice reports can
        be exported to CSV, XLSX, and PDF, while the annual invoice and cash report provides yearly billed and collected
        totals with CSV/XLSX export options.
    </p>

    <br />

</div>
